  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">QUERCUS &amp; AVES VI: HABITAT PROT, REST &amp; WEB TOOLS FOR BIRD CONS IN OAK HABITATS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will continue work to conserve oak habitats and their associated priority bird species in the Pacific Northwest. Specifically, conservation actions include the acquisition of over 100 acres on two properties in Wasco County, Oregon; habitat restoration on six sites in western Oregon and Washington; and development of OakBirdPop, an interactive web-based tool used to inform land managers of desired ratios of oak habitat types to achieve bird population objectives. Several species highly associated with oak habitats will benefit, including ash-throated flycatcher, black-throated gray warbler, blue-gray gnatcatcher, Cassins vireo, lazuli bunting, and western bluebird.</narrative>
  </description>
